1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,523
Guten Tag. This is Liam, in for Bear. Anthropic's claude code security review won't

2
00:00:04,543 --> 00:00:09,391
catch every security bug. It reads one pull request at a time, and only what

3
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:12,960
changed. So the real question is the risks this change adds.

4
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:17,599
A pull request: a proposed change, waiting for review before it's merged. The diff:

5
00:00:17,619 --> 00:00:22,517
just the lines a change adds or removes. And a false positive: a flagged problem

6
00:00:22,537 --> 00:00:23,500
that isn't real.

7
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:28,571
Here's a pull request: a crate on a belt, on its way to being merged. The security

8
00:00:28,591 --> 00:00:33,297
review is a GitHub Action, a job GitHub runs when a pull request opens. It puts

9
00:00:33,317 --> 00:00:35,660
Claude over the belt, as a security reviewer.

10
00:00:35,730 --> 00:00:40,344
Open the crate. Most of the repo stays behind. Only the changed files go under

11
00:00:40,364 --> 00:00:45,286
review. Claude can read the rest for context, but it's told to report only what this

12
00:00:45,306 --> 00:00:47,140
pull request adds, not old problems.

13
00:00:47,210 --> 00:00:51,979
The changed files pass under the scanner. Claude reads them for meaning, not just

14
00:00:51,999 --> 00:00:55,399
patterns, looking for things like injection, broken authentication, exposed secrets

15
00:00:55,419 --> 00:01:00,530
and weak crypto. Each suspect becomes a finding: the line, how serious, how it could

16
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:02,240
be exploited, and a fix.

17
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:07,104
Before anything is posted, a filter catches likely false positives. Hard rules drop

18
00:01:07,124 --> 00:01:11,917
low-impact kinds, like denial of service and rate limits. Then Claude re-checks each

19
00:01:11,937 --> 00:01:15,250
finding, and drops the ones it isn't confident in.

20
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:19,840
What's left lands on the pull request as review comments, pinned to the exact lines,

21
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:24,986
each with a thumbs up and a thumbs down. The prompt puts it plainly: better to miss

22
00:01:25,006 --> 00:01:27,710
a theoretical issue than flood you with false positives.

23
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:31,938
Then a person decides. The action posts a comment review. It doesn't approve the

24
00:01:31,958 --> 00:01:36,415
pull request, and it doesn't merge it. You read each comment, fix what's real, and

25
00:01:36,435 --> 00:01:37,310
dismiss what isn't.

26
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:42,130
You can also run the same review yourself. Claude Code ships a slash command, slash

27
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:46,582
security review, that reviews the pending changes on your branch. Copy it into your

28
00:01:46,602 --> 00:01:48,490
project, and you can tune it.

29
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:53,256
One caution, in the repo's own words: the action is not hardened against prompt

30
00:01:53,276 --> 00:01:58,310
injection. A pull request could carry text written to steer the reviewer. So run it

31
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:02,352
only on trusted pull requests, and have a maintainer approve outside contributors

32
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:03,700
before their workflows run.

33
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:07,781
Your turn. Paste this into Claude Code: Add Anthropic's claude code security review

34
00:02:07,801 --> 00:02:13,053
to this repo as a GitHub Action. Trigger it on pull requests only, read the API key

35
00:02:13,073 --> 00:02:17,084
from a repository secret, and exclude our vendored and generated folders. It must

36
00:02:17,104 --> 00:02:21,736
never run on untrusted pull requests, so tell me how to require approval for outside

37
00:02:21,756 --> 00:02:25,767
contributors. I'll treat its comments as leads to check, not verdicts. Then check

38
00:02:25,787 --> 00:02:30,729
two things yourself. Does the workflow run on pull requests only, with the key in a

39
00:02:30,749 --> 00:02:34,140
secret? And in your repo settings, do outside contributors need approval?

40
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:39,300
A Security Review on Every Pull Request. At Nik Bear Brown.
